{"name":"Cosy Blanket","hex":"#c3a598","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cosy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Affording comfort and warmth; snug; social and comfortable.","Warm and comfortable."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A padded or knit covering put on an item to keep it warm, especially a teapot or egg.","A padded or knit covering for any item (often an electronic device such as a laptop computer)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cosy"},{"term":"blanket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy, loosely woven fabric, usually large and woollen, used for warmth while sleeping or resting.","A covering layer of anything."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["General; covering or encompassing everything."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blanket"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blanket","blocks":[{"text":"A blanket is a swath of smooth cloth large enough either to cover or to enfold most of the user's body and thick enough to keep the body warm by trapping radiant body heat that otherwise would be lost through convection and radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Lautrec_in_bed_1893.jpg/330px-Lautrec_in_bed_1893.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blanket","wikidata":"Q5852"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Monet_dejeunersurlherbe.jpg/500px-Monet_dejeunersurlherbe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Monet_dejeunersurlherbe.jpg/500px-Monet_dejeunersurlherbe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Le déjeuner sur l'herbe, (right section) by Claude Monet","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonet_dejeunersurlherbe.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c